utritional support and comprehensive care, thereby promoting better recovery outcomes for patients.", "HOSPITAL STAY:Hospital stay refers to the duration a patient remains in the hospital following surgery. This duration can be influenced by various factors, including the patient's nutritional status and the implementation of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols. Additionally, nutritional support and interventions play a significant role in determining the length of time a patient spends in the hospital.", "READMISSION RATES:Readmission rates refer to the frequency of patients returning to the hospital after discharge, which can be affected by nutritional support and surgical protocols.", "COLON SURGERY:", "CANCER GÁSTRICO:Gastric cancer, a condition for which various nutritional screening methods have been compared", "PARÁMETROS ANTROPOMÉTRICOS:Measurements of the human body used to assess nutritional status, which have limitations in predicting surgical complications", "PARÁMETROS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional indicators such as albumin levels that are used in nutritional screening", "VALORACIÓN DE LA FUERZA MUSCULAR:An assessment of muscle strength that can be part of nutritional screening but has limited predictive value for surgical complications", "GRAVEDAD DE LA ENFERMEDAD:The severity of underlying health conditions that can affect nutritional status and surgical outcomes", "NUTRICIONAL RISK INDEX:", "SURGERY:Surgery is a medical procedure commonly utilized in the treatment of esophageal cancer. It plays a crucial role in managing the disease, but it also significantly impacts the nutritional status of patients. This impact can lead to complications, particularly in those who are malnourished. Therefore, careful management of nutrition and body composition is essential both before and after the operation to ensure optimal patient outcomes. Studies have highlighted the importance of nutritional support in the postoperative recovery of cancer patients undergoing surgery, emphasizing that such support may be necessary to mitigate potential complications and enhance recovery. Overall, surgery is a vital medical service that requires comprehensive care, including attention to the nutritional needs of patients.", "AYUNO PREOPERATORIO:AYUNO PREOPERATORIO refers to the practice of fasting prior to surgical procedures, which has been developed and refined over time to minimize the risk of complications during surgery. This preoperative fasting is recommended to ensure patient safety and improve surgical outcomes by preventing issues such as aspiration and other related complications.", "ANESTESIA:Anesthesia is a medical intervention used during surgery to prevent pain and awareness, influencing preoperative fasting guidelines."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}